<article class="entry entry-current">
  <h3 class="heading">Cross-platform performance prediction for HPC</h3>
  <p class="time"><strong>Texas State University</strong> · Aug 2023 – Present · Advisor: Dr. Tanzima Islam</p>

  <p>
    When an HPC application moves to a new supercomputer, how fast will it run? I build machine
    learning models that answer this from measurements taken on other systems, so people can pick
    a machine before they spend allocation time on it. This work is done with researchers at
    Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory.
  </p>

  <ul class="impact-list">
    <li>xAMM, an attention-based model for cross-platform prediction (CCGrid 2025).</li>
    <li>ModelX, transfer learning across heterogeneous performance datasets (HPDC 2025).</li>
    <li>Few-shot learning for relative performance prediction (COMPSAC 2024).</li>
  </ul>
</article>
